# The dependency list: upstream skills (mattpocock-skills) the pipeline uses
# and keeps. One name per line, each with a one-line comment on the line above
# saying who uses it. The upstream check confirms each still exists and that
# its disable-model-invocation flag is unchanged. Every name must exist
# upstream: never one of our own skills (to-plan is ours), and never a name on
# replaced-skills.list. guard.test.sh enforces all three.

# /artisan-agent:grill and /artisan-agent:triage sit on its questioning loop.
grilling
# /artisan-agent:grill and /artisan-agent:triage update GLOSSARY.md and ADRs through it.
domain-modeling
# /artisan-agent:craft, /artisan-agent:to-spec and /artisan-agent:to-plan slice into tickets with it.
to-tickets
# /artisan-agent:craft hands a map-shaped goal to it.
wayfinder
# /artisan-agent:implement builds test-first with it.
tdd
# /artisan-agent:implement and implement-plan review the diff with it.
code-review
# /artisan-agent:craft routes hard bugs to it.
diagnosing-bugs
# /artisan-agent:grill and wayfinder spike unknowns with it.
research
# /artisan-agent:grill and wayfinder prototype design questions with it.
prototype
# Kept per spec #44 for design-vocabulary work; no plugin skill calls it by name yet.
codebase-design
# Kept for skill-authoring: plugin skill edits follow it.
writing-for-agents
# Project setup and the ADR check write PR bodies through it.
pr
